                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had a surprisingly enjoyable time with Tibetan Quest: Beyond the World's End. The game has a nice adventure feel to it, and I liked moving between the different locations and figuring out what I was supposed to do next.\r\n\r\nThe hidden-object sections are fun without being too frustrating, and the puzzles are generally easy enough that I could keep the story moving without constantly needing hints.\r\n\r\nThe story isn't something I'll remember forever, but it works well for this type of game. Overall, it's a relaxing experience that I would recommend to anyone who enjoys casual point-and-click and hidden-object adventures.\r\n\r\nEnjoy :)",
